WEBVTT

00:21.210 --> 00:24.570
Looks like there's no one
left to defy us, big brother.

00:24.570 --> 00:28.670
This village now belongs to us,
the Three Orc Brothers.

00:28.880 --> 00:33.800
Yes. Let's raise a glass and have
a wild celebration, my little brothers.

00:33.800 --> 00:37.830
If we look over there, do you think
we'll find some humans still alive?

00:37.830 --> 00:39.960
We'll catch 'em alive and then...

00:39.960 --> 00:42.270
Something to look forward to.
Right, big brother?

00:42.270 --> 00:44.450
Sounds perfect!

00:55.290 --> 00:56.530
What's this?

00:56.530 --> 00:58.450
Who are you, kid?

01:02.240 --> 01:03.660
Ikusaba Asahi.

01:04.630 --> 01:05.920
Adventurer.

01:05.920 --> 01:07.540
"Adventurer"?

01:07.540 --> 01:09.990
You're gonna take us all on by yourself?

01:09.990 --> 01:13.420
A pipsqueak like you?
Against us, the Three Orc Brothers?

01:13.420 --> 01:17.380
It would be in your absolute
best interests not to attack me.

01:17.380 --> 01:18.760
What?!

01:18.760 --> 01:21.390
If you attack and regret it
after, it'll be too late.

01:21.820 --> 01:24.140
Do you understand? I've given you a warning.

01:25.030 --> 01:27.650
Don't come back as a ghost
and haunt me, you hear?

01:27.900 --> 01:30.360
That arrogance of yours sounds incurable...

01:31.340 --> 01:33.780
so I'll crush it for you, human!

01:44.180 --> 01:45.730
Big brother!

01:52.500 --> 01:53.840
Explode.

02:35.560 --> 02:37.170
I never imagined I'd do that.

02:39.570 --> 02:43.490
Save a child from a traffic accident, I mean.

02:45.140 --> 02:49.310
So it really does happen, huh? That thing
where your body suddenly moves on its own.

02:49.850 --> 02:50.850
Hang on.

02:50.850 --> 02:53.690
What is this? Am I dead?!

02:55.030 --> 02:57.280
That girl. She's safe.

02:58.280 --> 03:01.110
Well then, I guess it's okay.

03:01.930 --> 03:05.280
This counts as sort of a happy ending, right?

03:05.650 --> 03:11.030
Aw, man. That new <i>Armor's Core</i> game
didn't come out while I was still alive.

03:12.280 --> 03:14.750
Wonder if they have video
games in the next world.

03:15.530 --> 03:17.790
When they find out I'm dead,

03:17.790 --> 03:20.220
I wonder how everyone will react.

03:22.850 --> 03:24.270
Maya-nee.

03:25.410 --> 03:27.210
Wh-What's that light?

03:28.160 --> 03:30.240
It's not trying to pull me in, is it?

03:37.020 --> 03:38.170
Ow!

03:39.130 --> 03:40.370
Ow.

03:45.070 --> 03:45.780
Huh?

03:45.780 --> 03:47.400
Where am I?

03:48.010 --> 03:49.480
What was that?

03:51.460 --> 03:52.930
This is...

03:53.420 --> 03:55.210
Could it be?

03:57.710 --> 03:58.920
Wow!

03:58.920 --> 04:01.410
This is seriously like a village from an RPG!

04:01.410 --> 04:05.430
I've seen this before. It's like
a place in <i>Skyrom</i> or <i>Witser 3</i>!

04:05.880 --> 04:08.390
Then, there's <i>Dragon Search</i>, <i>Thors</i>...

04:08.390 --> 04:10.940
Oh, and it's sort of like
the Asobie Series, too!

04:10.940 --> 04:13.850
Lately, the FS series hasn't
really had anything like this.

04:13.850 --> 04:15.850
Oh, no, wait, XII did...

04:16.340 --> 04:17.980
Hey! Watch where you're walking!

04:17.980 --> 04:19.120
Oh, I'm sorry.

04:19.120 --> 04:21.240
Honestly. Be more careful.

04:22.900 --> 04:26.560
It looks like medieval Europe, but for
some reason, everyone speaks Japanese!

04:26.560 --> 04:27.870
That happens a lot.

04:29.050 --> 04:32.620
"Guild" and "shop" and "skill"!
Those words are all so familiar to me!

04:32.860 --> 04:37.140
And it's all in English and Japanese, meaning
everything's been completely localized.

04:37.550 --> 04:39.130
So what's going on?

04:39.450 --> 04:42.430
After getting into an accident,
I got sent into a game?

04:45.130 --> 04:47.590
I've been reincarnated!

04:51.100 --> 04:52.560
No, don't do that.

04:52.560 --> 04:56.100
I may be in another world,
but I have to act like the locals.

04:56.310 --> 04:58.610
First, I'll upload a picture.

04:58.610 --> 05:00.360
Yeah, makes sense.

05:00.360 --> 05:02.500
I don't know how to contact anyone,

05:02.500 --> 05:04.930
and I'm in an unfamiliar
world without any money.

05:05.860 --> 05:07.610
However!

05:10.980 --> 05:12.170
I'm a game otaku,

05:12.170 --> 05:16.000
and I've got most of the
popular isekai works down,

05:16.000 --> 05:18.970
so there's no crisis I can't get out of!

05:19.880 --> 05:22.590
Well, this is unusual.

05:22.590 --> 05:24.850
I've never seen these materials before.

05:24.850 --> 05:26.730
Is it from an ancient civilization?

05:26.730 --> 05:28.830
U-Um, something like that.

05:28.830 --> 05:31.060
All right. I'll buy it off you for 500 mani.

05:31.060 --> 05:33.620
So in the Japanese version
of this, "money" is "mani"!

05:33.620 --> 05:35.620
Yup, super easy to understand.

05:35.620 --> 05:37.500
"Japanese version"? What's that?

05:37.500 --> 05:39.310
Oh, uh, I was just talking to myself.

05:39.560 --> 05:43.320
So anyway, the weapons and
armor here are for sale, right?

05:43.320 --> 05:44.570
Well, yes.

05:44.830 --> 05:47.560
When you're low on money,
sell things you don't need.

05:47.880 --> 05:50.730
Then, use that money to get
equipment you will need.

05:50.730 --> 05:52.580
That's how the game world works.

05:55.890 --> 06:00.790
I prioritized physical agility, and chose
leather armor and a simple sword.

06:01.360 --> 06:02.710
Wow!

06:02.710 --> 06:04.920
So <i>this</i> is a real sword!

06:04.920 --> 06:09.640
Yeah, with my speed, the best place for me
is fighting in the front.

06:12.140 --> 06:15.140
All right! I am now fully equipped!

06:16.020 --> 06:17.140
Which means...

06:17.140 --> 06:20.710
the natural next step has gotta be this.

06:20.710 --> 06:22.100
Next.

06:22.100 --> 06:22.980
Right here.

06:23.770 --> 06:26.990
Thanks for waiting.
Are you looking for a quest?

06:26.990 --> 06:30.990
U-Um... This is my first time.

06:30.990 --> 06:33.340
Really? Your first time?

06:33.340 --> 06:34.540
Um, yeah.

06:34.540 --> 06:36.500
Feeling a little nervous?

06:36.500 --> 06:38.400
Y-Yeah, a little.

06:39.050 --> 06:40.000
That's so cute.

06:40.240 --> 06:43.260
Well then, for the young
man's first time,

06:43.260 --> 06:46.460
I'll take responsibility and
teach you all kinds of things.

06:46.710 --> 06:49.370
Let's see... I'm pretty sure
it was around here...

06:49.370 --> 06:52.310
Got it. First, there's the
adventurer registration form.

06:52.310 --> 06:54.970
Believe it or not, just by
writing your name on this form...

06:54.970 --> 06:58.980
The guild receptionist is a gyaru
who's nice to otaku. Sweet!

07:00.210 --> 07:01.010
Excuse me?

07:01.010 --> 07:03.230
I wish I'd had one as a friend growing up.

07:03.230 --> 07:05.510
Hey, are you even listening?

07:05.510 --> 07:07.150
Come on. Write your name here.

07:07.150 --> 07:08.990
Oh. Right. Sorry.

07:09.760 --> 07:10.760
Good, good.

07:10.760 --> 07:12.560
Ikusaba Asahi-kun, right?

07:12.890 --> 07:16.460
Now, let's pick your
very first quest together!

07:16.460 --> 07:17.490
Y-Yeah!

07:17.490 --> 07:19.180
If you're soloing your first quest,

07:19.180 --> 07:21.900
I recommend something
like hunting killer rabbits.

07:21.900 --> 07:26.360
They're an E on the danger ratings, so it's
a super simple hunting quest, but still...

07:26.360 --> 07:27.250
Okay, I'll do that.

07:27.720 --> 07:31.260
And so, in Ikusaba Asahi's second life...

07:31.260 --> 07:33.510
the first act begins now!

07:33.870 --> 07:36.260
There are times in life when
a person thinks such things.

07:37.390 --> 07:39.390
I once thought that way, too.

07:43.230 --> 07:48.150
Nope. No. Suddenly encountering a huge wyvern
as soon as I leave town?

07:50.360 --> 07:52.820
What's with this crappy game?!

07:55.450 --> 07:56.700
The difficulty setting...

07:57.050 --> 07:58.900
Someone must've set it to the wrong one!

07:58.900 --> 08:01.210
Whoa!

08:01.210 --> 08:03.080
Calm down.

08:05.250 --> 08:07.790
When it comes to game strategy,
the first thing you do is this.

08:07.790 --> 08:08.840
Status.

08:09.380 --> 08:12.590
Isn't there something? Everyone sent
to another world tends to have...

08:12.590 --> 08:14.110
a cheat skill!

08:17.350 --> 08:19.110
What about my base stats?

08:19.110 --> 08:20.100
That's tiny!

08:21.290 --> 08:22.560
Maybe I'm a villager?

08:25.210 --> 08:26.950
Fine. Now that it's come to this...

08:28.440 --> 08:30.400
Stone Throw!

08:30.400 --> 08:31.320
There!

08:33.930 --> 08:34.780
Right.

08:42.070 --> 08:43.120
Maya-nee.

08:44.000 --> 08:45.460
Maya-nee.

08:46.670 --> 08:51.090
Maya-nee!

09:05.500 --> 09:07.240
Did you call for your big sister?

09:07.240 --> 09:08.900
You did, didn't you, Asahi?

09:10.960 --> 09:12.320
Maya-nee.

09:22.840 --> 09:23.930
Maya-nee!

09:26.430 --> 09:28.040
My body feels so light.

09:28.040 --> 09:29.540
N-No damage?

09:30.920 --> 09:32.380
And what is this?

09:32.770 --> 09:35.100
Strength. Wisdom.

09:35.100 --> 09:36.470
They're surging up inside me!

09:37.940 --> 09:39.490
With this power...

09:39.490 --> 09:42.350
I can protect my little brother!

09:48.410 --> 09:50.440
W-With just one blow?

09:50.440 --> 09:52.250
That's a one-hit kill!

09:54.220 --> 09:55.430
Child's play.

09:55.430 --> 09:56.780
M-Maya-nee.

09:57.130 --> 09:59.780
Wh-Why's my big sister here
in this other world with me?

09:59.780 --> 10:02.150
Wait. It might be some kind of illusion.

10:02.150 --> 10:04.240
There's no telling what
goes on in this world, so—

10:04.240 --> 10:05.820
Asahi!

10:05.820 --> 10:08.580
Your big sis missed you!

10:09.750 --> 10:14.190
These handsome features!
This smooth skin! This huggable frame!

10:14.190 --> 10:16.800
And this wonderful scent
that tickles my nostrils!

10:16.800 --> 10:19.510
I am certain. This really is my little brother!

10:19.850 --> 10:22.390
So cute! You're just <i>too</i> cute, Asahi!

10:22.390 --> 10:24.100
Well, that seals it.

10:24.100 --> 10:26.270
This over-the-top, brother-obsessed girl...

10:26.270 --> 10:29.510
is unmistakably my real older sister. Yup.

10:30.760 --> 10:33.200
I see. So we're in another world?

10:33.200 --> 10:35.050
Fascinating.

10:35.050 --> 10:37.400
Why'd you end up here, too, Maya-nee?

10:38.410 --> 10:39.780
Thank you for asking.

10:39.780 --> 10:42.320
When you fell into a coma after the accident,

10:42.320 --> 10:44.680
as your big sister, I was
beside myself with worry.

10:45.040 --> 10:46.410
And do you know what happened?

10:46.410 --> 10:50.740
While you slept, you started talking
about this and that in another world,

10:50.740 --> 10:53.920
and from time to time,
you'd laugh as if you were having fun.

10:54.890 --> 10:56.650
That's when I formed a hypothesis.

10:56.990 --> 11:00.180
Perhaps your spirit had
traveled to a different world.

11:00.570 --> 11:02.330
Your instincts are sharp, Maya-nee.

11:02.330 --> 11:06.970
That's why I repeatedly bashed
my head against the wall to get here.

11:06.970 --> 11:08.600
So you just followed me into death?!

11:08.600 --> 11:13.390
Wait. Did you say something about
a coma? So I'm still alive over there?

11:13.390 --> 11:15.970
Yes. You haven't regained
consciousness, though.

11:17.110 --> 11:20.570
I see. Somehow, I feel really relieved.

11:21.360 --> 11:22.430
So do I.

11:23.120 --> 11:27.150
By the way, Maya-nee, why were you
so ridiculously strong back there?

11:27.150 --> 11:32.050
The power of a big sister's love for her
younger brother is mighty. That must be why.

11:32.050 --> 11:34.130
That doesn't really explain anything.

11:34.130 --> 11:36.130
It doesn't matter, does it?

11:36.730 --> 11:38.470
Come on. Let's go.

11:39.760 --> 11:40.840
Yeah.

11:41.510 --> 11:44.060
I guess my life in this
other world is already over.

11:44.400 --> 11:48.310
It was rough here at times,
but I'm a little reluctant to leave.

11:48.670 --> 11:50.770
Should we head back, Maya-nee?

11:51.430 --> 11:53.100
Back to our own world?

11:55.400 --> 11:57.090
And how do we do that?

11:57.820 --> 12:01.120
You followed me here without
knowing how to get back?!

12:01.120 --> 12:05.870
Of course! Ascertaining your safety
came first! Everything else is secondary.

12:05.870 --> 12:10.390
Now that this has happened, we siblings
should carve out new lives in this world!

12:11.960 --> 12:14.080
When my sister's like this, she's no joke.

12:14.460 --> 12:17.840
That's right. I'm not OP in this one.

12:18.500 --> 12:21.170
This is a story about my sister being OP.

12:30.100 --> 12:31.480
W-Wait!

12:31.480 --> 12:32.620
Please wait!

12:37.770 --> 12:41.030
As usual, you are absolutely
merciless, Maya-nee.

12:41.800 --> 12:44.030
How could I have possibly forgiven them?

12:47.120 --> 12:48.300
That's true.

12:49.810 --> 12:53.750
Maya-nee must be thinking
about all the villagers who died.

12:53.750 --> 12:57.940
Those orcs called you a pipsqueak!
An insult like that warrants death!

12:57.940 --> 12:58.750
<i>That's</i> your focus?!

12:59.530 --> 13:00.250
This is awful!

13:00.250 --> 13:01.510
Huh? Wh-What is it?
This is awful!

13:01.510 --> 13:03.280
You have a scrape on your right cheek!

13:03.280 --> 13:04.460
Huh? I do?

13:04.460 --> 13:07.760
Allowing your delicate,
porcelain-like skin to be blemished...

13:07.760 --> 13:09.350
I've lost the right to be your big sister!

13:09.350 --> 13:10.320
Goddamn!

13:10.320 --> 13:12.520
Aren't you valuing
my skin a little too highly?

13:12.520 --> 13:14.430
Right. We'll use an elixir.

13:14.430 --> 13:17.520
No! Most people save those
for taking on the final boss!

13:17.520 --> 13:18.490
Oh, really?

13:18.490 --> 13:20.980
A bit of spit is enough to heal up a scrape.

13:20.980 --> 13:23.250
Spit? I see.

13:25.850 --> 13:29.790
You want your big sister to lick you all over.
That's what you're saying, isn't it?

13:30.490 --> 13:32.990
Th-That's <i>not</i> what I'm saying.

13:32.990 --> 13:37.250
We're siblings, right? There's
nothing to be embarrassed about!

13:37.630 --> 13:40.040
My degenerate big sister is attacking me!

13:41.170 --> 13:43.160
Where are you touching me, Maya-nee?!

13:44.910 --> 13:47.680
Is the village safe now?

13:47.680 --> 13:49.340
I know the answer to that!

13:49.340 --> 13:52.900
That man killed the monsters for us!

13:55.410 --> 13:57.730
O mighty hero!

13:58.400 --> 14:01.200
Let us praise the mighty hero!

14:05.070 --> 14:08.850
Doesn't it seem like what you did
has somehow been attributed to me?

14:08.850 --> 14:13.770
And what's wrong with that? I'm so proud
to hear everyone cheering for my little brother!

14:17.760 --> 14:22.880
And, well, even though stuff like
this happens, I'm not OP in this one.

14:22.880 --> 14:25.510
This is a story about my big sister being OP.

14:26.410 --> 14:28.710
Or at least, that's what it's supposed to be.

14:28.710 --> 14:30.720
Congratulations, Asahi-kun!

14:31.320 --> 14:33.890
So, uh... What's this about?

14:33.890 --> 14:37.770
Your rank has gone up! You've leaped
from Rabbit Class to Ogre Class!

14:37.770 --> 14:40.100
Oh, adventurer ranks, huh?

14:40.100 --> 14:42.980
This is a huge, huge promotion for you!

14:42.980 --> 14:46.860
Rising so far up the ranks this quickly
is honestly unprecedented!

14:46.860 --> 14:48.170
I-Is it?

14:48.170 --> 14:51.140
Of course it is.
Now, hold out your hand for a sec.

14:51.140 --> 14:51.870
My hand?

14:52.090 --> 14:52.980
Like this?

14:53.450 --> 14:55.870
Here. Your Ogre Class badge.

14:56.700 --> 14:58.080
Isn't it great, Asahi-kun?

14:58.080 --> 14:59.530
Y-Yeah.

14:59.530 --> 15:01.080
I'll go ahead and explain.

15:01.540 --> 15:05.590
This badge is like an identity document
issued here in the royal capital.

15:05.590 --> 15:09.020
So you're not allowed to sell it
or give it to someone else.

15:09.020 --> 15:11.020
I-I would never do that!

15:11.020 --> 15:12.090
After all...

15:12.970 --> 15:17.100
I've never been showered
with this much praise before.

15:18.200 --> 15:21.290
Oh, and falsifying your
rank isn't allowed, either.

15:21.290 --> 15:22.600
Falsifying your rank?

15:22.600 --> 15:27.270
Going up ranks by pretending you're stronger
than you are is a serious crime.

15:27.690 --> 15:30.720
Pretending you're strong...
when you're actually weak?

15:31.600 --> 15:33.480
If you're found out,
worst case, you get this.

15:33.480 --> 15:34.620
This.

15:35.020 --> 15:38.180
Though, I don't need to worry about
<i>you</i> doing that, do I, Asahi-kun?

15:41.740 --> 15:42.920
Maya-nee, I'm begging you!

15:43.130 --> 15:47.070
Please hide your strength and
make it seem like I'm the strong one!

15:47.450 --> 15:49.550
I don't really understand, but sure.

15:49.550 --> 15:52.490
Oh, and let me check your stats.

15:52.490 --> 15:53.440
Stats?

15:53.440 --> 15:54.430
Your numbers.

15:54.430 --> 15:56.040
Well, I suppose.

15:56.040 --> 15:58.390
But only for you, Asahi,
because you're special.

15:58.390 --> 16:01.350
From top to bottom, they're 92, 58...

16:01.610 --> 16:03.340
I don't mean your measurements!

16:03.340 --> 16:05.830
Then, is it the number of
beauty marks on my body?

16:05.830 --> 16:09.170
Hold out your hand, say "Status,"
and a screen appears with your stats!

16:09.170 --> 16:10.410
Go on. Try it.

16:11.220 --> 16:12.050
Like this?

16:12.050 --> 16:13.200
Status.

16:14.260 --> 16:15.320
Let's see.

16:15.570 --> 16:17.760
It doesn't seem to be showing anything.

16:17.760 --> 16:20.010
That's strange. Is it some kind of error?

16:20.010 --> 16:22.830
And the whole screen seems weird somehow.

16:24.250 --> 16:25.330
It can't be!

16:25.330 --> 16:30.430
Her levels are so maxed out,
her ability scores stretch off the screen?!

16:32.120 --> 16:35.070
Why is it my sister that's
super strong and not me?

16:35.610 --> 16:38.960
You can't ever show your status
screen to <i>anyone</i>, understand?

16:38.960 --> 16:41.200
It's a secret just between the two of us, okay?

16:41.200 --> 16:43.140
A secret just between the two of us?

16:43.670 --> 16:44.810
I like it!

16:46.080 --> 16:47.010
Asahi.

16:47.880 --> 16:51.350
Your big sister wants to know
your secret numbers, too.

16:52.310 --> 16:54.280
For example...

16:54.780 --> 16:58.030
The number of beauty marks on your body.

16:58.030 --> 17:00.810
Let me count them!

17:02.430 --> 17:04.380
Siegfried-sama!

17:04.380 --> 17:06.250
Wh-What's going on?

17:06.250 --> 17:08.590
All of our hopes rest on you!

17:09.920 --> 17:12.870
Defeat the Demon King for us!

17:19.100 --> 17:21.810
I wonder what all that was about.
Are they famous?

17:21.810 --> 17:24.330
They're the strongest party: Clan Balmunc.

17:24.330 --> 17:26.740
Oh, it's you from the pawnshop.

17:26.740 --> 17:27.680
Hi.

17:29.210 --> 17:30.690
- Sieg-sama!
- Mimosa-san!

17:30.690 --> 17:33.570
What's the big parade for?

17:33.570 --> 17:38.680
It's a send-off parade. This is all for them,
before they head off to defeat the Demon King.

17:38.680 --> 17:42.040
A Demon King! So there's one in this world, huh?

17:42.040 --> 17:43.150
Demon King?

17:43.150 --> 17:44.940
The Demon King is the final boss.

17:44.940 --> 17:50.320
In isekai stuff, defeating the Demon King
can sometimes send you back to your own world.

17:50.320 --> 17:53.250
I see. Then, I'll go defeat
this person real quick.

17:53.250 --> 17:55.840
It's not like popping to the
convenience store, y'know.

17:56.690 --> 18:00.550
No matter how high your rank is right now,
you need to gain more experience.

18:01.290 --> 18:04.150
That's the leader of Balmunc,
Dragon Hunter Siegfried.

18:04.150 --> 18:07.060
He's a Dragon Class adventurer.

18:07.370 --> 18:08.730
Dragon Class?

18:08.730 --> 18:11.560
That's two ranks above Ogre Class.

18:11.560 --> 18:15.560
That's so cool.
I want to be like that one day.

18:18.780 --> 18:21.000
What's so great about being Dragon Class?

18:22.200 --> 18:24.210
I never liked that guy.

18:24.210 --> 18:26.540
He's a cocky little brat!

18:26.540 --> 18:30.000
What's so great about
Dragon Hunter Siegfried, anyway?

18:30.000 --> 18:32.840
E-Excuse me, sir. That's enough now, isn't it?

18:32.840 --> 18:33.460
What?
E-Excuse me, sir. That's enough now, isn't it?

18:33.780 --> 18:36.300
No one asked you!

18:39.130 --> 18:41.090
How could that guy do that?

18:41.090 --> 18:44.460
That Delivn. Soon as
Siegfried-san leaves town, he...

18:44.460 --> 18:47.020
Isn't there anyone who can stop him?

18:47.020 --> 18:48.830
He got demoted, but he used
to be Ogre Class, so...

18:48.830 --> 18:49.820
Father...
He got demoted, but he used
to be Ogre Class, so...

18:49.820 --> 18:51.480
He got demoted, but he used
to be Ogre Class, so...

18:51.480 --> 18:54.690
No, there's another Ogre Class right here.

18:54.690 --> 18:55.750
Hey!

18:55.750 --> 18:58.270
Oh! It's that guy who shot up the ranks!

18:58.270 --> 19:00.530
You're the boy genius
everyone's taking about, right?

19:00.530 --> 19:02.600
I'm sure he'll take care of this for us!

19:02.600 --> 19:03.990
E-Excuse me!

19:05.060 --> 19:08.450
Please avenge my father's food stand!

19:08.460 --> 19:10.870
Isn't that boy's name Ikusaba Asahi?

19:10.870 --> 19:13.460
Yeah. That's our brave champion, Asahi.

19:17.610 --> 19:19.860
Hold up! Why are they
expecting me<i> to do something?</i>

19:19.860 --> 19:22.220
If anyone finds out I'm weak, I'm doomed!

19:22.220 --> 19:26.810
What's this? A pipsqueak like you is gonna take me on?

19:27.530 --> 19:29.650
You belittled Asahi by
calling him a pipsqueak.

19:29.650 --> 19:30.980
Oh no! Oh no! Oh no!

19:31.270 --> 19:36.060
Maya-nee, if you go ham on a human,
it'll be like an R18-rated splatter film!

19:36.060 --> 19:39.440
Don't worry, Asahi. I possess good sense.

19:39.440 --> 19:40.450
Really?

19:40.450 --> 19:43.560
Yes! I'll pound him with magic
until he's on the brink of death.

19:43.560 --> 19:47.850
And for the rest of his life, he'll believe
a quick death would have been better!

19:47.850 --> 19:50.460
You don't have a single shred of good sense!

19:50.460 --> 19:53.110
What's wrong? You not gonna come at me?

19:53.110 --> 19:53.960
Maya-nee.

19:56.360 --> 19:57.540
That's a lot of trouble.

19:57.540 --> 19:59.710
After, I'll do anything you ask, all right?

19:59.710 --> 20:00.670
Anything?!

20:00.670 --> 20:02.320
You get it, right? Please?

20:02.320 --> 20:05.180
Hey, kid! What're you
whispering about over there?

20:06.130 --> 20:08.100
Stop bellyaching, boozehound.

20:09.430 --> 20:12.170
That's a disgraceful way for
a senior adventurer to behave.

20:12.170 --> 20:15.130
So because the young gun,
Siegfried, overtook you in rank,

20:15.130 --> 20:17.760
you lost your nerve and now
you just drown your sorrows, huh?

20:17.760 --> 20:19.440
Wh-What did you say?!

20:19.790 --> 20:22.400
Go home and suck on your mama's tiddies instead.

20:22.400 --> 20:25.310
You little brat!

20:43.170 --> 20:44.300
What the...

20:44.750 --> 20:45.990
Wanna get hit with that?

20:48.120 --> 20:50.220
This force hitting that body...

20:50.220 --> 20:52.270
Puh... Puh...

20:52.270 --> 20:55.190
Please spare me!

20:55.190 --> 20:56.750
As expected.

20:56.750 --> 20:57.690
Incredible!

20:57.690 --> 20:59.520
Thank you, Asahi-san!

20:59.770 --> 21:01.860
Wow! Hooray! That was amazing!

21:08.900 --> 21:11.160
It worked!

21:13.160 --> 21:15.460
Ah, everything worked out.

21:15.460 --> 21:19.670
No one found out I'm weak, and we drove off
that scoundrel without anyone getting hurt.

21:19.670 --> 21:22.130
For now, we can call this a happy ending.

21:22.910 --> 21:25.200
You've forgotten one thing, Asahi.

21:26.520 --> 21:28.090
You promised.

21:28.550 --> 21:31.060
A-ny-thing.

21:33.850 --> 21:37.440
And you'll keep that promise, Asahi!

21:37.440 --> 21:40.540
My life in another world
with my big sister begins.

21:40.540 --> 21:45.030
What kinds of events are
awaiting us on the road ahead?

23:26.850 --> 23:28.590
Another bust.

23:28.590 --> 23:30.510
I'm so bored.

23:31.170 --> 23:34.850
That overwhelming power
I sensed a few days ago...

23:35.470 --> 23:37.800
I can't wait to fight to the death

23:38.170 --> 23:40.180
with the owner of that aura.

23:45.020 --> 23:48.030
Next time: "You Call Me Your Sister?"
